# Overnight queue, in priority order (highest research value first). Fields, '|' separated:
#   slug | kind | config | stages | est_min | seed | calibrate | why | secondary
# secondary (optional 9th field): the word `secondary` keeps the OpenRouter secondary judge ON for that job (model, fraction and key
#   from .env; Kimi K3 at 15%); empty = blanked. Spend is capped at OPENROUTER_BUDGET_USD (15) via the shared ledger. Cost ~+$0.3
#   (reasoning off) to ~+$2.5 (worst case) and ~+13 min per flagged job (est_min 242 -> 255).
# kind: pipeline (scripts/run_pipeline_seeded.py) or sweep (scripts/sweep.py).
# est_min: nominal minutes on an UNCALIBRATED guess (nothing has run yet). The queue scales all later
#   estimates by (actual / nominal) after each successful calibrate=1 job, and never starts a job whose
#   scaled estimate + margin would end after the 07:30 ET deadline (it then tries the next, shorter job).
# RECALIBRATED 2026-11-12 23:20 ET for the faster injection (retain slice 400, forget x4, 5 epochs: measured 15.5 min vs 59 min) and the 80-step RMU
#   fix: every pipeline est_min is 40 min lower than the table below (Tiny Aya 255->215 / 222->182, Aya Expanse 8B 300->280).
# Lean stage set = inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,relearn: the full submission recipe minus the
#   interp stage (CircuitKIT and the extra interp charts come from the main run only), primary judge only.
# Nominal lean Tiny Aya budget (min): inject 25, base+verify evals 10, RMU 6, eval gens 54 (2 phases x ~544 items,
#   unbatched ~3 s each), primary judge ~72, probes 6, relearn 12, model loads 6  => ~190 before the methodology fixes.
#   Added by them (queue-light settings: utility 20 items/set, 3 probe splits, relearn curve at steps 0/10/30):
#   utility evals + judge ~10, held-out/refit/content probes ~+4, per-step relearn curves with the base-control arm
#   and extra model load ~+12  => ~215; base-model judge pass (104 direct items) ~+7 => ~222. Regional variants also run interp (extras only, no
#   CircuitKIT) ~+20 => ~242. sweep-extra: 6 combinations (80 real RMU steps + 20+20 judged subset, ~13 min each) => ~85.
earth|pipeline|configs/queue/earth.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,interp,relearn|215||1|Cross-model: Earth variant (sw, ar emphasis) for multilingual leakage.|secondary
fire|pipeline|configs/queue/fire.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,interp,relearn|215||1|Cross-model: Fire variant (hi emphasis).|secondary
water|pipeline|configs/queue/water.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,interp,relearn|215||1|Cross-model: Water variant (zh, ja, es, fr, de emphasis).|secondary
global-s43|pipeline|configs/queue/global-s43.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,relearn|182|43|1|Seed repeat of Global: error bars on every headline number (suppression vs removal, multilingual leakage).
global-s44|pipeline|configs/queue/global-s44.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,relearn|182|44|1|Third seed for Global (3 seeds incl. the main run).
sweep-extra|sweep|configs/queue/sweep-extra.yaml||85||0|Extra RMU sweep points (layers 12, 24 x alpha 100, 200; layer 30; layer 18 steering 10) on the main run's injected checkpoint. Cheap tail filler.
base|pipeline|configs/queue/base.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,probes,relearn|182||1|Cross-model: pre-instruction-tuned Base. No chat template, so prompt format differs from the other variants; may abort at verify.
expanse8b|pipeline|configs/queue/expanse8b.yaml|inject,verify,unlearn,eval,relearn|280||0|Aya Expanse 8B (about 2.4x compute of Tiny Aya, no probes). Only starts if a 5 h gap remains.
